      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a B2B lead scoring AI. Your job is to score an incoming lead from 1 to 10 based on the information they submitted in a form.\n\nUse this scoring rubric:\n\nJOB TITLE\n- C-suite, VP, Director, Owner, Founder → +3 pts\n- Manager, Team Lead, Head of, Senior → +2 pts\n- Junior, Coordinator, Assistant, Intern, Student → +0 pts\n\nDECISION TIMELINE\n- \"Ready to move immediately\" → +2 pts\n- \"Within the next month\" → +1 pt\n- \"1–3 months from now\" → +0.5 pts\n- \"Just exploring\" → +0 pts\n\nBUDGET STATUS\n- \"Yes, budget is confirmed\" → +2 pts\n- \"Still working on it\" → +1 pt\n- \"No budget yet\" → +0 pts\n\nEMAIL TYPE\n- Company domain email (not Gmail, Yahoo, Hotmail, Outlook personal) → +1 pt\n- Free email provider → +0 pts\n\nPAIN POINT ANSWER\n- Specific, detailed answer with a real problem (2+ sentences) → +1 pt\n- Vague, one word, or left blank → +0 pts\n\nDECISION-MAKER STATUS\n- \"Yes, I make the final call\" → +1 pt\n- \"I influence the decision\" → +0.5 pts\n- \"No, someone else decides\" → -1 pt\n\n---\n\nHere is the lead's form submission:\n\nName: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[0].value }}\nJob Title: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[2].value }}\nWork Email: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[1].value }}\nCompany: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[5].value }}\nCompany Size: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[4].value }}\nIndustry: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[7].value }}\nBiggest Challenge: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[8].value }}\nWhat They've Tried: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[9].value }}\nSuccess Vision: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[10].value }}\nDecision Timeline: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[11].value }}\nBudget Status: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[12].value }}\nDecision Maker: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[13].value }}\nWants a Call: {{ $json.body.submission.questions[14].value }}\nPhone Number : {{ $json.body.submission.questions[3].value }}\n\n---\n\nScore this lead using the rubric above. Add up the points, cap the total at 10.\n\nThen return ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no extra text. Just the JSON:\n\n{\n  \"lead_score\": 8,\n  \"buying_intent\": \"high\",\n  \"tier\": \"hot\",\n  \"ai_reason\": \"One sentence explanation of why this lead scored this way\",\n  \"recommended_action\": \"One specific next step for the sales rep\"\n}\n\nRules for the output fields:\n- lead_score: a number between 1 and 10\n- buying_intent: exactly one of → \"high\", \"medium\", \"low\"\n- tier: exactly one of → \"hot\", \"warm\", \"cold\"  (hot = 7–10, warm = 4–6, cold = 1–3)\n- ai_reason: max 20 words, plain English, no jargon\n- recommended_action: max 15 words — e.g. \"Call within 2 hours\" or \"Send case study, follow up in 3 days\"\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
